    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d153">

                <pb facs="0383" n="69" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg69"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/570</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Roumania</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Vopicka</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Bucharest</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1914-08-21T16:00:00+01:44">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">August 21, 1914, 4 p.m.</hi>
                    </date>
                    <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received August 22, 2:45 p.m.</hi>] </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p> Talaat Bey and President of Chamber are here to induce Roumania to join Turkey
                    in favor of Austria and Germany. It seems unlikely that Roumania will join
                    Turkey as Roumania evinced she is strong enough to act independently.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Vopicka</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
